This package contains the V1.0 source release of Anteater Chess,
including source code, tests, build scripts, and documentation.
The program is a complete C implementation of standard chess with
a GTK+ 3 graphical interface.

Directory overview:
- src/
  Source files (organized by module: ai/, control/, core/,
  error/, event/, gameplay/, input/, log/, time/, turn/, ui/)
- include/
  Header files
- tests/
  Unit tests
- bin/
  Build output directory for the executable, runtime logs,
  and test binaries
- build/
  Build intermediates and source-package staging area
- doc/
  User manual and software specification
- assets/
  SVG piece images and icons used by the GUI

Supported Makefile targets:
- make / make all
  Build bin/chess (GUI, requires GTK+ 3) and create bin/logs
- make test
  Build and run the full test suite
- make clean
  Remove generated build artifacts while preserving the bin/ layout
- make tar
  Generate Chess_V1.0_src.tar.gz
- make tar-user
  Generate the user/customer package Chess_V1.0.tar.gz

After building, run the program with:
   ./bin/chess

Build outputs:
- bin/chess
  Main GUI executable
- bin/logs/
  Runtime log directory
- bin/tests/
  Test binaries and test temporary files

For installation details see INSTALL.
For gameplay instructions see doc/Chess_UserManual.pdf.
For module-level architecture see doc/Chess_SoftwareSpec.pdf.
